                        "cot": "\n\nBefore nap time, a kindergarten teacher typically:\n\n1. Encourages children to use the bathroom and wash their hands.\n2. Helps children settle down and transition from playtime to nap time.\n3. Provides a quiet and calming environment by dimming the lights, playing soft music, and closing curtains or blinds.\n4. Reads a story or sings a lullaby to help children relax and feel comfortable.\n5. Checks on each child to ensure they are comfortable and have everything they need for nap time.\n6. Monitors the room to ensure that children are resting quietly and not disturbing others.\n7. Wakes children up gently when nap time is over and helps them transition back to playtime.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) encourage.",
