                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Mad cow disease is the most likely answer to how someone can die from eating hamburger. Mad cow disease, also known as bovine spongiform encephalopathy (BSE), is a fatal neurological disease that affects cattle. If a cow infected with BSE is slaughtered and its meat is used to make hamburger, humans who consume the contaminated meat can contract the disease. The disease can cause severe neurological symptoms and ultimately lead to death. While gas, getting full, feeling full, and death are not specific to hamburger consumption, they may be related to other factors such as overeating or digestive issues.",
