                        "cot": "\n\nWhen someone is dead, they stop being alive, which eliminates option D. \n\nBreathing also stops when someone is dead, so option C is correct. \n\nMoving and working may or may not stop when someone is dead, depending on the circumstances, so options A and B are not necessarily true. \n\nThere is no such thing as \"deadworks,\" so option E is not correct. \n\nTherefore, the answer is C) breathing.",
