                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe answer is C) breathing.\n\nWhen someone dies, their body stops functioning. This means that their heart stops beating, their brain stops functioning, and their lungs stop breathing. Breathing is a vital function of the body that is necessary to sustain life. Without breathing, the body cannot receive oxygen, which is necessary for the cells to function properly. Therefore, when someone is dead, they stop breathing. \n\nOption A) Moving: While it is true that the body becomes still and motionless after death, this is not the defining characteristic of death. Some movements, such as muscle twitches, can occur after death due to chemical reactions in the body.\n\nOption B) Working: This is a vague term and could refer to many different bodily functions. However, as mentioned above, when someone dies, their body stops functioning altogether.\n\nOption D) Alive: This is the opposite of being dead and does not provide any specific information about what bodily function stops when someone dies.\n\nOption E) Deadworks: This is not a commonly used term and does not provide any information about what bodily function stops when someone dies.",
                        "answers": [
