                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nDrinking alcohol can lead to various effects on the body and mind. Some of the possible outcomes are:\n\n1. Have fun: While drinking alcohol, some people may experience a sense of relaxation, euphoria, or socialization, which can be perceived as having fun.\n\n2. Intoxication: Alcohol is a central nervous system depressant that can impair cognitive and motor functions, alter mood and behavior, and lead to a state of intoxication. This can cause slurred speech, impaired judgment, loss of coordination, and other symptoms.\n\n3. Vomiting: Drinking too much alcohol can irritate the stomach lining and trigger a reflex to expel its contents, leading to vomiting.\n\n4. Drinking more alcohol: Alcohol can be addictive, and some people may develop a tolerance to its effects, which means they need to drink more to achieve the same level of intoxication. This can lead to a cycle of drinking more alcohol and increasing the risk of alcohol-related problems.\n\n5. Nausea: Similar to vomiting, alcohol can cause nausea and discomfort in the stomach, especially if consumed on an empty stomach or mixed with other substances that can irritate the digestive system.",
