                        "cot": "it is important to note that having a family member with melanoma does increase one's risk of developing the disease. Additionally, this patient's ethnicity and frequent travel to the Caribbean may also increase her risk. \n\nThe most common type of melanoma in African-Americans is acral lentiginous melanoma, which typically presents on the palms, soles, or under the nails. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Acral lentiginous. \n\nDesmoplastic melanoma is a rare subtype that presents as a firm, flesh-colored or pink nodule. Nodular melanoma is a rapidly growing, darkly pigmented lesion. Lentigo maligna melanoma typically occurs in older individuals with a history of sun exposure and presents as a flat, tan or brown lesion. Superficial spreading melanoma is the most common type overall and typically presents as an irregularly shaped, darkly pigmented lesion.",
