                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step:\n\n1. The mass is in the uterus, so it's likely to be a uterine mass.\n2. The mass is heteroechoic, meaning it has both echogenic and anechoic areas.\n3. The mass has numerous anechoic spaces.\n4. There is no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid.\n\nBased on these findings, the most likely cause of the mass is a corpus luteum cyst.",
