                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert.\n\n1) Chocolate cysts: These are typically found in endometriosis and are not associated with an enlarged ovary.\n\n2) Corpus luteum cysts: These are typically found in the postpartum period and are not associated with an enlarged ovary.\n\n3) Yolk sac tumor: This is a malignant tumor and is associated with an enlarged ovary.\n\n4) Theca leutein cysts: These are typically found in pregnancy and are associated with an enlarged ovary.\n\nTherefore, the most likely cause of the ovarian findings is theca leutein cysts.",
