                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nE) Theca lutein cysts\n\nThe presence of multiple thin-walled, septated cysts with clear content in both ovaries is highly suggestive of theca lutein cysts. These cysts are associated with high levels of human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), which can occur in conditions such as molar pregnancy, multiple gestation, or ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome. The intrauterine heteroechoic mass with numerous anechoic spaces and no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid is consistent with a molar pregnancy. Chocolate cysts are a type of endometriotic cyst and would not present with clear content. Corpus luteum cysts are typically simple cysts with thick walls and would not present with multiple septations. Yolk sac tumors and luteomas of pregnancy are rare and unlikely to present with the described findings.",
