                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe laboratory is investigating whether the ribosome can recognize a mischarged amino acid and still be incorporated into the growing peptide. They have biochemically charged a Lys-tRNA with valine instead of lysine and inserted the tRNA into the cell. They have designed an mRNA sequence that contains only codons for lysine. Based on this information, we can reason as follows:\n\n- The ribosome reads the mRNA sequence and matches each codon with the corresponding tRNA carrying the appropriate amino acid.\n- In this case, the ribosome encounters a codon for lysine and expects to see a Lys-tRNA carrying lysine. However, the laboratory has inserted a mischarged Lys-tRNA carrying valine instead.\n- There are two possible outcomes: either the ribosome recognizes the mischarged tRNA and prevents its incorporation, or it does not recognize it and incorporates it into the growing peptide.\n- Option A suggests that the ribosome recognizes the mischarged tRNA and removes the valine. However, this is unlikely because the ribosome does not have proofreading capabilities for tRNA charging errors.\n- Option B suggests that the ribosome recognizes the inappropriately inserted valine residue and terminates protein translation. This is also unlikely because the ribosome does not have a mechanism to detect mischarged tRNAs during translation.\n- Option D suggests that the mischarged tRNA will be degraded by the proteasome. However, the proteasome is not involved in tRNA degradation.\n- Option E suggests that the mischarged tRNA will be removed by the lysyl-tRNA synthetase. This is also unlikely because lysyl-tRNA synthetase is responsible for charging tRNAs with lysine, not for removing mischarged tRNAs.\n\nTherefore, the most likely outcome is option C: the mischarged tRNA with valine will be incorporated in the codons that specify for lysine. This means that the ribosome will not recognize the mischarged tRNA and will incorporate valine instead of lysine into the growing peptide. This could potentially affect the structure and function of the resulting protein.",
