                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nThe first step is to come up with a differential diagnosis. In this case, the patient has severe, unremitting pain. The differential diagnosis for this patient includes:\n\n-Cancer\n-Infection\n-Inflammation\n-Nerve damage\n\nThe next step is to order the appropriate tests to confirm the diagnosis. In this case, the patient has metastatic lung cancer. The appropriate tests to confirm this diagnosis would include:\n\n-Imaging (CT scan or MRI)\n-Biopsy\n\nThe next step is to treat the patient. The most likely recommended agent for this patient would be ketamine. Ketamine is an NMDA-receptor antagonist that can reduce the patient's opioid need.",
