                        "cot": "it is important to understand what a LOD score is. A LOD (logarithm of odds) score is a statistical measure used to determine the likelihood of two loci being linked on a chromosome. A LOD score of 3 or higher is generally considered significant evidence for linkage, while a LOD score of less than 3 is considered suggestive but not conclusive evidence for linkage.\n\nIn this case, the fact that a novel mutation in the CFTR gene is found in a particular population suggests that this mutation may be closely linked to the \u0394F508 mutation. Therefore, we would expect to see a high LOD score if these two loci are indeed closely linked.\n\nBased on the answer choices given, the most likely option that suggests a high probability of linkage is D) LOD Score > 3. A LOD score of greater than 3 would provide strong evidence for linkage between the two loci, indicating that the novel mutation is likely located near the \u0394F508 mutation on the same chromosome.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "eaa71298-833b-425c-b64a-d2f112e796cc",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
