                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nIf the two loci (the \u0394F508 mutation and the novel mutation) are closely linked, then they are likely to be inherited together more often than not. This means that if an individual has one of the mutations, they are more likely to also have the other mutation. \n\nThe LOD score is a statistical measure used to determine the likelihood of two loci being linked. A LOD score of less than 1 suggests that the two loci are not likely to be linked, while a LOD score of greater than 3 suggests strong evidence for linkage. \n\nTherefore, the answer is B) LOD Score < 3. This suggests that there is some evidence for linkage, but it is not strong enough to definitively conclude that the two loci are closely linked.",
