                        "cot": "\n\nC) Microcytic red blood cells\n\nThalassemia intermedia is a type of thalassemia that results in a moderate decrease in the production of beta-globin chains. This can lead to the production of smaller and fewer red blood cells, which are known as microcytic anemia. Therefore, the blood smear of a patient with this mutation would be expected to show microcytic red blood cells. Macrocytic red blood cells (A) are associated with vitamin B12 or folate deficiency, while hyperchromic red blood cells (B) are associated with conditions such as pernicious anemia or hemolytic anemia. Bite cells (D) are associated with G6PD deficiency, and ringed sideroblasts (E) are associated with sideroblastic anemia.",
