                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-02",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe patient has a history of binge eating and purging behavior --> the physician should avoid prescribing a medication that would trigger or worsen those behaviors. \n\nDuloxetine, trazodone, and citalopram are all SSRIs, which have been shown to increase the risk of binge eating and purging behavior in patients with a history of those disorders. \n\nBupropion, on the other hand, is an antidepressant that actually decreases the risk of binge eating and purging behavior. \n\nTherefore, the physician should avoid prescribing duloxetine, trazodone, or citalopram, and should instead prescribe bupropion.",
