                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient has a gene defect that has caused dysfunction in a transmembrane protein, resulting in several hospitalizations for respiratory infections. The fact that he has thick purulent sputum suggests that he has a chronic respiratory infection. Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a common pathogen that causes chronic respiratory infections in patients with cystic fibrosis, which is also a genetic disorder that affects transmembrane proteins. Therefore, the most likely pathogen to infect this patient in adulthood is B) Pseudomonas.",
