                                "answer": " B. Pericardiocentesis is a procedure used to remove fluid from the pericardial sac. This procedure is indicated when the patient is experiencing symptoms of cardiac tamponade, which is a condition in which the pressure in the pericardial sac is increased due to the accumulation of fluid. Symptoms of cardiac tamponade include difficulty breathing, chest pain, and sinus tachycardia. In this case, the patient is exhibiting sinus tachycardia and the inability to palpate the radial pulse during inspiration, which are both signs of cardiac tamponade. Therefore, the next step in management should be to perform a pericardiocentesis.",
