                    {
                        "id": "5522336b-36cb-4bcc-835a-aabaf4e25a4d",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to consider the possible causes of the patient's symptoms. The enlarged cardiac silhouette on chest radiograph suggests the possibility of cardiac tamponade, which is a medical emergency that requires immediate intervention. The absence of palpable radial pulse during inspiration is known as pulsus paradoxus, which is a classic sign of cardiac tamponade.\n\nThe next step in management of this patient should be B) Pericardiocentesis. This involves the insertion of a needle or catheter into the pericardial sac to drain the accumulated fluid and relieve the pressure on the heart. This procedure can be life-saving and should be performed as soon as possible in patients with suspected cardiac tamponade.\n\nIV Heparin (A) is not indicated in this case, as it is used to prevent blood clots and is not effective in treating cardiac tamponade.\n\nChest CT scan (C) may be useful in diagnosing the cause of the cardiac tamponade, but it is not the first-line intervention in a patient with suspected cardiac tamponade.\n\nPericardial window (D) is a surgical procedure that involves creating a permanent opening in the pericardium to drain the fluid. This is a more invasive procedure than pericardiocentesis and is usually reserved for cases where pericardiocentesis is not effective.\n\nInserting a chest tube (E) is not the correct intervention in this case, as it is not effective in draining the pericardial fluid.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3f1940ae-b371-490e-a4d2-523b75e2537c",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Pericardiocentesis.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
