                    {
                        "id": "ea4cd9fc-956a-4fb8-b4a1-13a1a621b849",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient in the scenario has been brought to the emergency room after a motor vehicle accident. An EKG shows sinus tachycardia and chest radiograph reveals an enlarged cardiac silhouette. While observing sinus tachycardia on the patient's telemetry, the radial pulse cannot be palpated during inspiration. This suggests that the patient may be suffering from cardiac tamponade, a medical emergency in which fluid accumulates in the pericardial sac and compresses the heart, leading to decreased cardiac output.\n\nThe next step in management of this patient should be to perform a pericardiocentesis, which involves inserting a needle through the chest wall and into the pericardial sac to drain the fluid. This procedure can be life-saving in cases of cardiac tamponade, as it relieves the pressure on the heart and allows it to function properly.\n\nIV Heparin, chest CT scan, pericardial window, and chest tube insertion are not appropriate management options for cardiac tamponade. IV Heparin is used to treat blood clots, not cardiac tamponade. A chest CT scan may be useful in diagnosing the cause of the tamponade, but it is not a treatment option. A pericardial window is a surgical procedure that involves creating a permanent opening in the pericardium to drain fluid, but it is not typically performed in an emergency setting. Chest tube insertion may be used to drain fluid from the pleural space, but it is not effective in treating cardiac tamponade.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4123274c-82d0-41dd-9de1-28a311e37f14",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Pericardiocentesis.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/14 15:13:01",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
