                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-02",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\n1) The patient has decreased radial pulses, delayed capillary refill, and a distended abdomen. This suggests that the patient has decreased cardiac output. \n2) A decreased cardiac output would lead to decreased systemic vascular resistance. \n3) A decreased cardiac output would also lead to increased fractional tissue oxygen extraction. \n4) A decreased cardiac output would lead to increased carotid baroreceptor firing activity. \n5) A decreased cardiac output would lead to decreased cardiac inotropy. \n\nTherefore, the answer is D) Cardiac inotropy.",
                        "answers": [
