                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nThe first thing to consider is the patient's history. He drinks 10-12 beers daily and has not seen a physician in 15 years. This suggests that he might have a chronic liver disease. \n\nThe next thing to consider is the patient's current condition. He is vomiting blood and has black specks in his vomit. This suggests that he might have gastrointestinal bleeding. \n\nThe next thing to consider is the patient's physical examination. He has decreased radial pulses, delayed capillary refill, multiple spider angiomata, and a distended abdomen. This suggests that he might have portal hypertension. \n\nThe final thing to consider is the patient's vital signs. He has a temperature of 36.7\u00b0C (98.1\u00b0F), pulse of 122/min, and blood pressure of 85/59 mm Hg. This suggests that he might be in shock. \n\nIn conclusion, the most likely decreased in this patient in response to his current condition compared to a healthy adult is systemic vascular resistance.",
