                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " This patient has recurrent vomiting that began 5 hours ago. He describes the vomitus as bloody and containing black specks. He drinks 10\u201312 beers daily and has not seen a physician in 15 years. He appears pale. His temperature is 36.7\u00b0C (98.1\u00b0F), pulse is 122/min, and blood pressure is 85/59 mm Hg. Physical examination shows decreased radial pulses, delayed capillary refill, multiple spider angiomata, and a distended abdomen. He is oriented to person but not to place or time.\n\nThe most likely cause of this patient's condition is gastrointestinal bleeding. This can be due to a number of causes, including ulcers, cancer, or trauma.\n\nThe most likely decreased parameter in this patient is cardiac output. This is due to the decreased blood pressure and the increased pulse rate. The other parameters are not likely to be decreased in this patient.",
