                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is presenting with symptoms of dry eyes and mucosal ulceration, which are characteristic of Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome. The biopsy of the lower lip also shows lymphocytic infiltration of the minor salivary glands, which is a hallmark of Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome. Therefore, the most likely antibody to be seen in this patient is Anti-Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome type B (SS-B) antibody, which is commonly found in patients with Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome. \n\nA) Anti-Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome type B (SS-B) antibody - Correct\nB) Anti-centromere antibody - Not associated with Sj\u00f6gren's syndrome\nC) Anti-Jo-1 antibody - Associated with polymyositis/dermatomyositis\nD) Anti-Scl-70 antibodies - Associated with systemic sclerosis\nE) Anti-double stranded (-ds)DNA - Associated with systemic lupus erythematosus",
