                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient presents with infertility, which suggests a problem with his reproductive system. However, the fact that he has a history of cleft lip and recurrent upper respiratory infections as a child, as well as a silent cardiac auscultation, suggests that there may be a systemic issue at play.\n\nThe fact that cardiac auscultation is silent in the left 5th intercostal space at the midclavicular line suggests that there may be a problem with the heart, specifically with the closure of the mitral valve. This is a characteristic finding in individuals with Marfan syndrome, which is caused by a mutation in the gene encoding fibrillin-1, a microfibril-associated glycoprotein.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Microtubule monomeric protein. None of the other answer choices are associated with Marfan syndrome or mitral valve prolapse.",
