                    {
                        "id": "17684164-7907-4997-aefe-1339533a461c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "the silent cardiac auscultation in the left 5th intercostal space at the midclavicular line suggests a possible absence of the left ventricular impulse, which is a characteristic finding in individuals with Kartagener syndrome. Kartagener syndrome is an autosomal recessive disorder that affects the structure and function of cilia, leading to recurrent respiratory infections, situs inversus, and infertility in males due to immotile sperm. The mutation in Kartagener syndrome affects the microtubule-associated dynein arm, which is responsible for the movement of cilia and flagella. Therefore, the correct answer is D) Retrograde cytoskeletal motor protein.",
                        "answers": [
