                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The first thing we need to do is look at the patient's symptoms and figure out what's going on. The patient has back pain that is worse after moving furniture and walking, and he feels numbness and weakness in his legs. This suggests that the patient may have a problem with his spine. Next, we need to look at the patient's past medical history. The patient has osteoporosis, which means that his bones may be weak and more likely to break. The patient also has diabetes, which can cause nerve damage. Finally, the patient has a 44 pack-year smoking history, which means that he has been exposed to a lot of tobacco smoke over the years. This can also cause damage to the spine. Based on the patient's symptoms and past medical history, the most likely diagnosis is a compression fracture.",
