                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient is a previously healthy 35-year-old woman.\nShe has a sudden onset of weakness of her right arm and leg.\nShe has a history of cigarette smoking.\nShe has a normal temperature.\nShe has a normal pulse.\nShe has a normal blood pressure.\nShe has decreased muscle strength on the right side.\nDeep tendon reflexes are 4+ on the right.\nBabinski sign is present on the right.\nThe left lower leg is swollen, erythematous, and tender to palpation.\n\nThe correct answer is E) Carotid artery dissection.\n\nCarotid artery dissection is a tear of the intima of the carotid artery, most commonly at the site of atherosclerotic plaque. It is a cause of stroke in young patients and is associated with high mortality and morbidity.\nPatent foramen ovale is a small opening between the right and left atria of the heart.\nAtrial myxoma is a tumor that grows on the atria of the heart.\nMitral valve vegetation is an abnormal growth on the mitral valve of the heart.\nAtrial fibrillation is an abnormal heart rhythm characterized by rapid, chaotic electrical activity in the atria.\nA carotid artery dissection is a tear of the intima of the carotid artery, most commonly at the site of atherosclerotic plaque. It is a cause of stroke in young patients and is associated with high mortality and morbidity.",
