                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-02",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe first thing that stands out is that the patient has suddenly developed weakness on the entire right side of her body. This suggests that there is some sort of neurological issue going on. The next thing to note is that the patient has a fever. This could be indicative of an infection, which could potentially be the cause of the neurological issue. The next thing to note is that the patient has recently returned from a trip to Europe. This could be indicative of a travel-related illness, which could potentially be the cause of the neurological issue. The next thing to note is that the patient is a smoker. This could be indicative of a smoking-related illness, which could potentially be the cause of the neurological issue. The next thing to note is that the patient is taking an oral contraceptive. This could be indicative of a hormonal imbalance, which could potentially be the cause of the neurological issue.\n\nBased on the above information, it is most likely that the cause of the neurological issue is a travel-related illness.",
