                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step:\n\n1) The patient has increased tiredness and lethargy for the past 4 weeks. This suggests that she has anemia.\n\n2) Investigations show her hemoglobin level to be 8.6 gm/dL and serum creatinine of 4.6 mg/dL. This suggests that she has renal failure.\n\n3) The serum is negative for antinuclear antibodies (ANA) and positive for C3 nephritic factor. This suggests that she has a primary renal disease.\n\n4) Urinalysis shows a 3+ proteinuria. This suggests that she has a proteinuric renal disease.\n\n5) The renal biopsy demonstrates hypercellular glomerulus with electron dense deposits along the glomerular basement membrane. This suggests that she has a primary glomerular disease.\n\nThe most likely cause of the patient's condition is membranous glomerulonephritis (MGN).",
