                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is B) Addition of bupropion.\n\nCitalopram is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI) commonly used to treat anxiety and depression. However, one of the common side effects of SSRIs is sexual dysfunction, including decreased libido and difficulty achieving or maintaining an erection. Therefore, lowering the citalopram dose or switching to another SSRI like fluoxetine may not necessarily improve the patient's sexual dysfunction.\n\nBupropion is an antidepressant that works by increasing the levels of dopamine and norepinephrine in the brain. It has been shown to improve sexual function in patients with SSRI-induced sexual dysfunction. Therefore, adding bupropion to the patient's current treatment regimen may be an appropriate step in managing his sexual dysfunction.\n\nSildenafil, a phosphodiesterase type 5 inhibitor, is used to treat erectile dysfunction but may not be effective in this case since the patient's sexual dysfunction is likely due to SSRI-induced sexual dysfunction rather than primary erectile dysfunction.\n\nSelegiline is a monoamine oxidase inhibitor used to treat depression and Parkinson's disease but is not typically used to treat SSRI-induced sexual dysfunction.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "1acca211-9b74-4558-ba39-d792caac057e",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Addition of bupropion.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
