                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) Duodenal peptic ulcer.\nDuodenal peptic ulcer is the most likely diagnosis in this case. The patient has epigastric discomfort and cramping pain for the past 2 hours, mostly after meals and often subside several hours after she finishes eating. These episodes occur mostly after meals and often subside several hours after she finishes eating. She has lost a few pounds in the last couple of months. She is a smoker and drinks alcohol occasionally. Past medical history is insignificant except for chronic knee pain, for which she takes over the counter painkillers. Her temperature is 37\u00b0C (98.6\u00b0F), respiratory rate is 16/min, pulse is 77/min, and blood pressure is 120/89 mm Hg. A physical abdominal exam is unremarkable, including examination of the abdomen.",
