                        "cot": " \n\nThe patient has epigastric discomfort and cramping pain that occurs mostly after meals and often subsides several hours after eating. This points to a diagnosis of peptic ulcer disease.\n\nThe patient is a smoker and drinks alcohol occasionally, which are risk factors for peptic ulcer disease.\n\nThe patient has lost a few pounds in the last couple of months, which is another symptom of peptic ulcer disease.\n\nBased on the information given, the most likely diagnosis is peptic ulcer disease.",
