                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe first thing to note is that the infant is tachypneic and has blue-grey discoloration of the lips, fingers, and toes, which is a symptom of cyanosis. \n\nThe most likely cause of the cyanosis is a closure of the ductus arteriosus, which is a blood vessel that normally allows blood to bypass the lungs. If the vessel closes, it can cause cyanosis.",
