                        "cot": "Closure of the ductus arteriosus can cause cyanosis. The ductus arteriosus is a muscular tube that connects the right and left atriums of the heart. The ductus arteriosus is closed by the pulmonary artery. The ductus arteriosus is closed by the inhaled medication. The answer: B.",
