                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) Closure of the ductus arteriosus\n\nThe most likely cause of the infant's cyanosis is closure of the ductus arteriosus. The inhaled medication that increases smooth muscle cGMP is likely a prostaglandin E1 analog, which is used to keep the ductus arteriosus open in newborns with certain congenital heart defects. When the ductus arteriosus closes, blood flow to the lungs is decreased, leading to hypoxemia and cyanosis. The other answer choices are not related to the closure of the ductus arteriosus and are not likely causes of cyanosis in this case.",
