                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what's happening here. \n\nThe microbiologist has isolated several colonies of Escherichia coli on an agar plate. This means that the agar plate has a bunch of different E. coli colonies on it, each with their own unique genetic makeup. \n\nThe microbiologist exposes the agar plate to ciprofloxacin, which destroys all of the bacteria except for one surviving colony. This means that the ciprofloxacin must have killed all of the other E. coli colonies on the agar plate, except for the one that survived. \n\nThe most likely mechanism of antibiotic resistance in the surviving colony is that the colony has a mutation in its DNA gyrase. This mutation makes the DNA gyrase resistant to the ciprofloxacin, and allows the colony to survive.",
