                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Echocardiogram\n\nGiven the patient's symptoms of difficulty breathing, cough, and history of a previous heart attack, an echocardiogram would be the most appropriate next step in management. This test can help evaluate the function of the heart and identify any potential issues such as heart failure or valve problems. The ECG and chest X-ray may also provide additional information, but an echocardiogram would be the most specific test for evaluating the heart in this case. Angiography, CT, stress test, and cardiac biopsy may be considered later depending on the results of the echocardiogram and further evaluation. The patient's alcohol consumption should also be addressed as it can worsen heart failure and other cardiac conditions.",
