                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the patient's symptoms and medical history.\nThe patient has a severe cough, difficulty breathing, and experiences shortness of breath and coughing at night. He has a history of a heart attack and continues to consume alcohol despite medical advice.\n\nStep 2: Review the available diagnostic tests.\nThe patient has an ECG and chest X-ray available.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most likely diagnosis.\nBased on the patient's symptoms and medical history, the most likely diagnosis is heart failure.\n\nStep 4: Choose the appropriate next step in management.\nThe most appropriate next step in management for a patient with suspected heart failure is an echocardiogram. This test can help confirm the diagnosis and assess the severity of the condition. Angiography, CT, stress test, and cardiac biopsy may be useful in other situations, but are not the first-line tests for heart failure.",
