                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The patient has a severe cough and difficulty breathing, which suggests that he has some sort of respiratory infection. The fact that he has to sit down and rest after taking a few steps also suggests that he is not getting enough oxygen to his muscles. The fact that he has a cough that is persistent enough to wake him up from sleep suggests that he may have asthma or some other chronic lung disease. The fact that he has had a heart attack in the past suggests that he may have heart disease. The fact that he is still consuming alcohol despite his doctor's advice suggests that he may have liver disease. The next step in this patient's management would be to order a chest X-ray to see if there is any evidence of pneumonia or other lung disease.",
                        "answers": [
