                    {
                        "id": "86d347f4-d0ba-410c-9a47-7da79eaf65cc",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is presenting with symptoms of severe cough and difficulty breathing, especially at night, which suggests a respiratory issue. However, the fact that he has a history of a heart attack and continues to consume alcohol on a regular basis raises concerns about his cardiovascular health. \n\nThe electrocardiogram (ECG) and chest X-ray can provide valuable information about the patient's heart and lungs. The ECG can detect any abnormalities in the heart's electrical activity, while the chest X-ray can reveal any signs of fluid buildup or inflammation in the lungs. \n\nGiven the patient's symptoms and medical history, the next step in his management should be to perform an echocardiogram. This test uses ultrasound waves to create images of the heart and can help identify any structural abnormalities or functional issues that may be contributing to the patient's symptoms. \n\nAngiography, computed tomography (CT), stress test, and cardiac biopsy may be useful in certain cases, but they are not the most appropriate next step in this patient's management. Angiography and CT are imaging tests that can help diagnose blockages or other issues in the blood vessels, but they may not be necessary if the echocardiogram reveals no significant cardiac issues. A stress test is used to evaluate the heart's response to physical activity, but the patient's severe cough and difficulty breathing make it unlikely that he would be able to perform the test. Cardiac biopsy is a more invasive procedure that involves taking a small sample of heart tissue for analysis, and it is typically reserved for cases where other tests have been inconclusive. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Echocardiogram.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "ac1108d2-ca05-490e-9d52-3e8255595b83",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Echocardiogram.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
