                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-09",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is presenting with symptoms of shortness of breath, cough, and difficulty breathing, which are suggestive of a respiratory or cardiac issue. He has a history of a heart attack and continues to consume alcohol despite medical advice. The lab reports, ECG, and chest X-ray may provide some clues to the underlying cause of his symptoms. \n\nOption A, angiography, is a diagnostic test that involves injecting a contrast dye into the blood vessels to visualize any blockages or narrowing. While this may be useful in evaluating the patient's cardiac status, it is not the first-line test in this scenario.\n\nOption B, computed tomography (CT), is a type of imaging test that uses X-rays to create detailed images of the body. It may be useful in evaluating the lungs or heart, but again, it is not the first-line test.\n\nOption C, echocardiogram, is a non-invasive test that uses sound waves to create images of the heart. It can help evaluate the structure and function of the heart, including any abnormalities that may be causing the patient's symptoms. This is a reasonable next step in the patient's management.\n\nOption D, stress test, is a test that involves monitoring the heart's response to exercise or medication. It can help evaluate the patient's cardiac function and identify any abnormalities that may be causing the symptoms. However, given the patient's severe symptoms, it may not be safe to perform a stress test at this time.\n\nOption E, cardiac biopsy, is a procedure that involves taking a small sample of heart tissue for analysis. It is typically reserved for cases where other tests have been inconclusive and there is a suspicion of a specific cardiac condition. It is not indicated in this scenario.\n\nTherefore, the most appropriate next step in this patient's management is C) echocardiogram.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f8af7dcd-acf7-4e0e-bd81-6a8f885a2664",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Echocardiogram.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
