                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) Defect in WASP gene\nB) Defect in ATM gene\nC) Adenosine deaminase deficiency\nD) NADPH oxidase deficiency\nE) Defect in BTK gene\nThe correct answer is A) Defect in WASP gene.\nThis patient has a defect in the WASP gene, which is associated with immunodeficiency. The most common clinical manifestation of this condition is recurrent bacterial infections, and the patient also has failure to thrive and chronic diarrhea. The thymic shadow is absent because the thymus is not properly developed. The lymph node biopsy demonstrates the absence of germinal centers, which is another finding in this condition.",
