                        "cot": " The patient has a productive cough and shortness of breath, with a temperature of 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and respirations of 32/min. Crackles are heard over the right upper and the entire left lung fields. Sputum culture confirms infection with Streptococcus pneumoniae. Despite appropriate therapy, the patient dies.\n\nThe photomicrograph of a section of the lung obtained during the autopsy shows an arrow pointing to a cell-type.\n\nThe most likely mediator responsible for the presence of the cell-type indicated by the arrow is Interleukin-10 (IL-10). IL-10 is an anti-inflammatory cytokine that is released by immune cells in response to infection. It helps to regulate the immune response and reduce inflammation.",
