                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient presents with aching pain in her left leg that has progressively gotten worse over several days. She has a history of systemic lupus erythematosus and one spontaneous abortion. On physical examination, her left leg appears pink and slightly swollen, and Homan\u2019s sign is positive. A Doppler ultrasound reveals a thrombus in the left popliteal vein. Her lab results show a normal platelet count, a normal prothrombin time, and a prolonged partial thromboplastin time that corrects with mixing, indicating a factor deficiency. \n\nBased on these findings, the most likely cause of the patient\u2019s condition is an antiphospholipid antibody syndrome (APS), which is a common complication of systemic lupus erythematosus. APS is characterized by the presence of antibodies directed against phospholipids, which are components of cell membranes and play a key role in the coagulation cascade. These antibodies can cause a hypercoagulable state, leading to the formation of blood clots in the veins and arteries. \n\nThe positive Homan\u2019s sign and the presence of a thrombus in the left popliteal vein are consistent with deep vein thrombosis (DVT), which is a common manifestation of APS. The normal platelet count and prothrombin time rule out other causes of DVT, such as disseminated intravascular coagulation or a platelet disorder. The prolonged partial thromboplastin time that corrects with mixing suggests a factor deficiency, which is also a common finding in APS. \n\nIn summary, the most likely cause of the patient\u2019s condition is antiphospholipid antibody syndrome, which is characterized by the presence of antibodies directed against phospholipids and can cause a hypercoagulable state leading to DVT.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "2292fbfd-f255-4ed0-b330-6cf7aa09aa45",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Antibodies directed against phospholipids.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
