                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nFirst, the physician considers treatment with raloxifene. This medication would put her at increased risk of developing which of the following conditions?\n\nThe medication would put her at increased risk of developing pulmonary embolism, cellulitis, breast cancer, or hypercholesterolemia.\n\nPulmonary embolism is a condition in which a blood clot blocks the pulmonary artery or one of its branches. This can cause shortness of breath, chest pain, and even death.\n\nCellulitis is a bacterial infection of the skin and underlying tissue. It can cause redness, swelling, and pain.\n\nBreast cancer is a cancer that starts in the breast. It can cause a lump in the breast, changes in the nipple, and changes in the skin of the breast.\n\nHypercholesterolemia is a condition in which there is too much cholesterol in the blood. This can lead to heart disease.",
