                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step:\n\n1. The patient has chest pain that is somewhat similar to the chest pain that initially brought him into the hospital.\n\n2. The patient has a pulse of 86/min, respiratory rate of 16/min, and a blood pressure of 146/90 mm Hg.\n\n3. Auscultation of the chest reveals no abnormal findings.\n\n4. The patient's ECG is difficult to interpret.\n\nThe most likely diagnosis is that the patient is experiencing a recurrent myocardial infarction. An abnormal result on a troponin T test would be the most diagnostic utility in this case.",
                        "answers": [
