                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is presenting with chest pain, which could indicate a recurrence of his myocardial infarction. Therefore, a laboratory test that would help diagnose a myocardial infarction would be the most useful. The most specific and sensitive marker for myocardial infarction is troponin T, so the correct answer is E) Troponin T. Alanine aminotransferase and alkaline phosphatase are liver enzymes and would not be useful in diagnosing a myocardial infarction. Creatine kinase (CK-MB) and lactate dehydrogenase are markers for muscle damage, but they are not as specific for myocardial infarction as troponin T.",
                        "answers": [
