                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe man's behavior of accusing his wife of flirting with the waiter and questioning her fidelity suggests that he is projecting his own feelings of guilt and attraction towards his female co-workers onto his wife. Projection is a psychological defense mechanism in which a person attributes their own unacceptable thoughts, feelings, or impulses onto someone else. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Projection. \n\nDisplacement involves redirecting one's emotions or impulses from the original target to a substitute target. Dissociation involves a detachment from reality or a separation of mental processes. Reaction formation involves expressing the opposite of one's true feelings. Repression involves pushing unacceptable thoughts or memories into the unconscious mind. While some of these defense mechanisms may be related to the man's behavior, projection is the most consistent with his actions of accusing his wife of infidelity.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "b0c26221-ef2c-4963-9242-916dd476a902",
