                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Displacement: This defense mechanism involves transferring feelings from one target to another that is considered less threatening. In this case, the man is not transferring his feelings to another target, so this option is not correct.\n\nB) Dissociation: This defense mechanism involves a person disconnecting from their thoughts, feelings, or sense of identity. The man in this scenario is not disconnecting from his thoughts or feelings, so this option is not correct.\n\nC) Projection: This defense mechanism involves attributing one's own unacceptable thoughts, feelings, or motives to another person. In this case, the man is accusing his wife of cheating and being flirtatious when he himself is flirting with co-workers. This option seems to fit the scenario.\n\nD) Reaction formation: This defense mechanism involves behaving in a way that is opposite to one's true feelings. The man in this scenario is not behaving in a way that is opposite to his true feelings, so this option is not correct.\n\nE) Repression: This defense mechanism involves unconsciously blocking out painful or unacceptable thoughts or feelings. The man in this scenario is not blocking out his thoughts or feelings, so this option is not correct.\n\nBased on the analysis, the man's actions are most consistent with the psychological defense mechanism of Projection (C).",
