                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step. \n\nThe first thing to notice on the ECG is the irregularity of the QRS complexes. This suggests that the patient is not in sinus rhythm. The next thing to notice is that some of the QRS complexes are very wide, while others are narrow. This suggests that the patient has a ventricular arrhythmia.\n\nThe most likely diagnosis is ventricular tachycardia.",
