r choice is unlikely.\nD) Positive RPR, VDRL, and FTA-ABS: These are tests for syphilis, which can cause genital ulcers and lymphadenopathy. However, the presentation in this patient is not typical for syphilis, and these tests may not be positive in the early stages of the disease. This answer choice",
