 is caused by the bacterium Treponema pallidum. This condition presents with a painless, ulcerative lesion (chancre) at the site of infection, which can progress to systemic symptoms such as rash, fever, and lymphadenopathy. Syphilis is a common STI worldwide, but the patient's recent travel and sexual history make other STIs more likely.",
