                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert: \n\n1) Urge incontinence: This is an overactive bladder condition that can be caused by pregnancy and delivery. However, it is not a common complication of a third-degree laceration. \n\n2) Vesicovaginal fistula: This is an abnormal opening between the bladder and the vagina that can be caused by childbirth. However, it is not a common complication of a third-degree laceration. \n\n3) Fecal incontinence: This is the inability to control bowel movements. It can be caused by damage to the anal sphincter, which is a muscle that helps to control bowel movements. A third-degree laceration can damage the anal sphincter and cause fecal incontinence. \n\n4) Stress incontinence: This is the leakage of urine when coughing, sneezing, or laughing. It can be caused by damage to the pelvic floor muscles or the urethra. A third-degree laceration can damage the pelvic floor muscles or the urethra and cause stress incontinence. \n\nThe correct answer is D) Stress incontinence.",
