                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the patient's most likely form of diabetes is type 2 diabetes, given his age, obesity, and gradual onset of symptoms. \n\nThe correct answer is E) Unrelated to his abdominal obesity. While obesity is a major risk factor for developing type 2 diabetes, it is not directly related to the underlying pathophysiology of the disease. Type 2 diabetes is characterized by insulin resistance and impaired insulin secretion, which can be influenced by genetic and environmental factors. HLA class II gene makeup (A) is associated with type 1 diabetes, while pancreatic islet cell amyloid deposition (B), pancreatic islet cell leukocyte infiltration (C), and auto-antibodies against pancreatic islet cell antigens (D) are all associated with autoimmune forms of diabetes, such as type 1 diabetes or latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA).",
