isorder. The patient's elevated episodes may qualify as hypomanic, and her recurrent episodes of depressed mood may not meet the criteria for major depressive episodes. Additionally, her medical history and occasional marijuana use may contribute to her mood symptoms. However, further evaluation and monitoring would be necessary to confirm this diagnosis.",
