                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe drug that should be administered to this patient for medical abortion of her 6-week pregnancy is D) Mifepristone.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The patient is a 24-year-old woman who had intercourse for the first time a few weeks ago and missed her menstrual period two weeks ago. She took several over the counter pregnancy tests that confirmed her pregnancy.\n- The patient is tearful about the pregnancy and is very concerned. After extensive conversations with her physician and counseling, she decides she wants to medically abort her 6-week pregnancy.\n- Medical abortion is a procedure that uses medication to end a pregnancy. It is an alternative to surgical abortion and can be done up to 10 weeks of pregnancy.\n- The drug that is commonly used for medical abortion is a combination of mifepristone and misoprostol. Mifepristone is a progesterone receptor antagonist that blocks the action of progesterone, a hormone that is necessary for the maintenance of pregnancy. Misoprostol is a prostaglandin analog that causes uterine contractions and expulsion of the pregnancy.\n- Megestrol is a progestin that is used to treat breast cancer and appetite loss in people with HIV/AIDS. It is not used for medical abortion.\n- Tamoxifen is a selective estrogen receptor modulator that is used to treat breast cancer and prevent breast cancer in people at high risk. It is not used for medical abortion.\n- Terbutaline is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist that is used to treat asthma and premature labor. It is not used for medical abortion.\n- The copper intrauterine device (IUD) is a long-acting reversible contraceptive that can be used for up to 10 years. It is not used for medical abortion.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Mifepristone.",
