                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "we can identify that the patient is experiencing symptoms of aphasia, which is a language disorder that can result from damage to various areas of the brain. The weakness in the right arm suggests that there may also be some motor involvement.\n\nBased on the symptoms described, the most likely location of damage is the left frontal lobe, which is responsible for language production and expression. The left internal capsule is also a possibility, as it contains fibers that connect the frontal lobe to other areas of the brain involved in language processing. However, the fact that the patient is physically frustrated suggests that he is aware of his communication difficulties, which is more indicative of damage to the frontal lobe.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Left frontal lobe.",
