                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is experiencing sudden onset speech changes and weakness of the right arm. This suggests a stroke, which is a disruption of blood flow to the brain. The fact that the speech changes are random and disconnected suggests damage to the language centers of the brain. The language centers are primarily located in the left hemisphere of the brain, so we can eliminate options D and E. \n\nThe weakness of the right arm suggests damage to the motor pathways that control the right side of the body. These pathways pass through the internal capsule, which is a narrow band of white matter that connects the cerebral cortex to the brainstem. Therefore, the most likely location of damage is the left internal capsule, which is option B. \n\nOption A (left frontal lobe) and option C (left temporal lobe) are also involved in language processing, but they do not explain the weakness of the right arm. Therefore, option B is the best answer.",
                        "answers": [
