                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Option E is the best answer.\nAs a healthcare professional, it is your duty to do no harm and to respect your patient's autonomy. If a patient has a living will or other advanced directive that specifies that they do not want to receive a blood transfusion for religious reasons, you must respect their wishes. Even if you believe that the patient's decision is wrong or will result in their death, you must respect their autonomy and follow their instructions.\n\nOption A is incorrect because it violates the patient's autonomy and does not respect their wishes.\n\nOption B is incorrect because it does not address the immediate medical issue and is a non-actionable step.\n\nOption C is correct because it respects the patient's wishes and follows their instructions.\n\nOption D is incorrect because it violates the patient's autonomy and does not respect their wishes.\n\nOption E is incorrect because it violates the patient's autonomy and does not respect their wishes.",
