                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nOption E is not ethical as it goes against the principle of beneficence, which requires healthcare professionals to act in the best interest of the patient. Therefore, refusing to treat the patient is not an option.\n\nOption B is a good idea, but it may take time to convene the ethics board, and the patient may not have that much time. Therefore, it is not the best option in this scenario.\n\nOption D is not ethical as it puts the burden of decision-making on the wife, who may not be equipped to make such a decision. It is the responsibility of the healthcare professional to make the best decision for the patient.\n\nOption C is not the best option as it goes against the principle of beneficence. The healthcare professional has a duty to save the patient's life, and a blood transfusion is necessary to achieve that goal.\n\nTherefore, the best option is A, to administer a blood transfusion to save the patient's life. The healthcare professional should explain the situation to the patient's wife and try to convince her of the importance of the blood transfusion. If she still refuses, the healthcare professional should respect her decision but make sure that all other options have been exhausted before doing so.",
