                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-09",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient has a history of travel, which suggests that he may have been exposed to an infectious agent that is not commonly found in his home country. He also has symptoms of fever, cough, headache, and diarrhea, which are consistent with an infectious disease. The chest radiograph shows patchy infiltrates in both lungs, which suggests that the infectious agent has spread to the respiratory system. The mild hyponatremia and mild elevation of AST/ALT levels suggest that the patient's liver and kidneys may be affected by the infection.\n\nA) Can form an endospore: This characteristic is associated with bacterial spores, which are resistant to heat, radiation, and chemical disinfectants. However, not all bacteria can form spores, and spore-forming bacteria are not necessarily associated with the patient's symptoms.\n\nB) Has a rabbit reservoir: This characteristic suggests that the infectious agent is commonly found in rabbits and may be transmitted to humans through contact with rabbit feces, urine, or saliva. However, there is no mention of the patient having contact with rabbits, and the symptoms are not consistent with a rabbit-borne disease.\n\nC) Has no cell wall: This characteristic is associated with some bacteria, such as Mycoplasma, which are able to survive without a cell wall. However, these bacteria are not commonly associated with the patient's symptoms.\n\nD) Is more common in parrot owners: This characteristic suggests that the infectious agent is commonly found in parrots and may be transmitted to humans through contact with parrot feces, urine, or saliva. However, there is no mention of the patient having contact with parrots, and the symptoms are not consistent with a parrot-borne disease.\n\nE) Is transmitted by air conditioning: This characteristic suggests that the infectious agent is transmitted through the air conditioning system, which can spread the agent to multiple people in a closed space. However, there is no mention of other people in the patient's environment having similar symptoms, and the symptoms are not consistent with an air conditioning-borne disease.\n\nThe correct answer is B) Has a rabbit reservoir.",
