                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step. A Type I error is when you reject the null hypothesis when it is actually true. In this case, the null hypothesis would be that mepolizumab has no effect on reducing asthma exacerbations. So if the authors had made a Type I error, it would mean that they found that mepolizumab was effective in reducing asthma exacerbations when it actually was not. \n",
