                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of fluid entering it - This statement is true. Oncotic pressure is the pressure exerted by proteins in the blood plasma, which tends to pull water into the circulatory system. As fluid is filtered out of the glomerular capillaries, the concentration of proteins in the remaining fluid increases, leading to an increase in oncotic pressure.\n\nB) Glucose concentration in the capillaries is the same as that in glomerular filtrate - This statement is true. Glucose is freely filtered through the glomerular capillaries, and its concentration in the filtrate is the same as that in the blood plasma.\n\nC) Constriction of afferent arteriole decreases the blood flow to the glomerulus - This statement is true. The afferent arteriole is the blood vessel that supplies blood to the glomerulus. Constriction of this vessel will decrease the blood flow to the glomerulus, leading to a decrease in glomerular filtration rate.\n\nD) Hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of the fluid entering it - This statement is not true. Hematocrit is the percentage of red blood cells in the blood. Since red blood cells are not filtered through the glomerular capillaries, the hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries should be the same as that of the fluid entering it.\n\nSo, the correct answer is D) Hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of the fluid entering it.",
