                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe flat topped violaceous papules suggest a diagnosis of lichen planus. The thinning of nails and onycholysis suggest involvement of the nails. \n\nThe microscopic finding observed in lichen planus is acantholysis, which is the separation of the epidermal cells from each other. This results in the formation of a subepidermal cleft or blister. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Acantholysis.",
