                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Birth asphyxia: Estimation of blood sugar is relevant in cases of birth asphyxia because it can cause hypoglycemia (low blood sugar) in newborns.\n\nB) Large for date baby: Estimation of blood sugar is relevant in cases of large for date baby because they are at risk of developing hypoglycemia due to increased insulin production.\n\nC) Baby of hypothyroid mother: Estimation of blood sugar is relevant in cases of baby of hypothyroid mother because hypothyroidism can cause hypoglycemia in newborns.\n\nD) Rh Incompatibility: Estimation of blood sugar is not directly relevant in cases of Rh incompatibility. Rh incompatibility can cause hemolytic disease of the newborn, which can lead to anemia and jaundice, but not necessarily hypoglycemia.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Rh Incompatibility.",
