                        "cot": "A) Birth asphyxia - Estimation of blood sugar is relevant because hypoglycemia can be a consequence of birth asphyxia.\n\nB) Large for date baby - Estimation of blood sugar is relevant because large for date babies are at risk of hypoglycemia due to increased insulin production.\n\nC) Baby of hypothyroid mother - Estimation of blood sugar is not directly relevant in this case, as hypothyroidism in the mother does not typically cause blood sugar abnormalities in the baby.\n\nD) Rh Incompatibility - Estimation of blood sugar is relevant because Rh incompatibility can lead to hemolytic anemia, which can cause hypoglycemia in the baby.\n\nSo, the correct answer is C) Baby of hypothyroid mother.",
