                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Histopathological examination for Negri bodies. \n\nNegri bodies are eosinophilic, intracytoplasmic inclusions found in the neurons of the brain and spinal cord of animals infected with rabies virus. The presence of Negri bodies in the corneal impression is a definitive diagnosis of rabies. Indirect immunofluorescence and antibodies against rabies virus can also be used for diagnosis, but they are not as specific as the presence of Negri bodies. PCR for virus can detect the presence of viral RNA, but it may not be as sensitive as histopathological examination for Negri bodies.",
