                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the scenario and the symptoms presented by the patient. The patient has come after a dog bite with hydrophobia, tearing, and altered sensorium. These symptoms are suggestive of rabies.\n\nStep 2: Corneal impression has been taken. Corneal impression is a diagnostic test used to detect the presence of rabies virus in the cornea of the eye.\n\nStep 3: Identify the most accurate test for the diagnosis of rabies virus. The options given are:\n\nA) Indirect immunofluorescence: This test is used to detect the presence of antibodies against the rabies virus in the patient's blood. It is not the most accurate test for the diagnosis of rabies.\n\nB) PCR for virus: Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a molecular diagnostic test used to detect the presence of viral DNA in the patient's sample. This test is highly accurate and can detect the virus even in low concentrations. It is a good option for the diagnosis of rabies.\n\nC) Histopathological examination for Negri bodies: Negri bodies are eosinophilic, cytoplasmic inclusions found in the neurons of the brain and spinal cord of animals infected with rabies virus. Histopathological examination of brain tissue can detect the presence of Negri bodies, which is a confirmatory test for the diagnosis of rabies. However, this test is invasive and requires brain tissue, which is not always available.\n\nD) Antibodies against Rabies virus: This test is similar to indirect immunofluorescence and is used to detect the presence of antibodies against the rabies virus in the patient's blood. It is not the most accurate test for the diagnosis of rabies.\n\nStep 4: Based on the above analysis, the most accurate test for the diagnosis of rabies virus is PCR for virus (Option B).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) PCR for virus.",
