                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The prodromal stage is the period before the rash appears. The eruptive stage is the period when the rash is present. Therefore, the isolation period of measles is from the onset of the prodromal stage until the 7th day of the rash. The answer is D) Eruptive stage until 7th day of rash.",
