                        "cot": "\n\nC) Glucuronyl transferase deficiency\n\nThis is because a high level of direct bilirubin indicates impaired conjugation of bilirubin in the liver, which is the function of glucuronyl transferase. Rotor syndrome and Gilbert syndrome both have elevated indirect bilirubin levels, while primary biliary cirrhosis typically presents with elevated levels of both direct and indirect bilirubin.",
