                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What are the embryonic germ layers?\nThe embryonic germ layers are the three primary layers of cells that form during embryonic development. They give rise to all the tissues and organs of the body.\n\nStep 2: Where do the embryonic germ layers come from?\nThe embryonic germ layers are derived from the inner cell mass of the blastocyst, which is a hollow ball of cells that forms about 5 days after fertilization.\n\nStep 3: What is the epiblast and hypoblast?\nThe inner cell mass of the blastocyst is divided into two layers: the epiblast and the hypoblast. The epiblast gives rise to the embryo proper, while the hypoblast gives rise to the yolk sac.\n\nStep 4: Which layer(s) give rise to the embryonic germ layers?\nThe ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm are all derived from the epiblast. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm from epiblast; endoderm from hypoblast.",
