                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe epiblast and hypoblast are the two layers that form during the early stages of embryonic development. The epiblast gives rise to the embryo proper, while the hypoblast forms the yolk sac. \n\nThe three germ layers (ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm) are formed during gastrulation, which is the process by which the embryo folds in on itself to form a three-layered structure. \n\nDuring gastrulation, cells from the epiblast migrate inward to form the mesoderm and endoderm, while the remaining cells form the ectoderm. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm from epiblast; endoderm from hypoblast.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c3acd933-c2dc-491c-be0a-6521252593a4",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
